  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while Image (ResNet50, single profile) only reaches 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality by a wide margin. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether multiprofile aggregation provides meaningful additional signal over a single profile, or whether the encoder is the bottleneck. This experiment tests whether moving from single to multiprofile with the same PCA encoder and the simplest aggregation (avgpool) improves on the RNA baseline. It is the most direct, minimal extension of the best result (config_001), isolating the effect of profile multiplicity. If multiprofile helps, it opens a path to test transformer aggregation (config_003); if it does not, it redirects attention toward encoder quality (scvi/scgpt). With 7 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information next step for improving the dominant modality."
